# googleapis/release-please-action

Automates CHANGELOG generation, GitHub releases, and version bumps by parsing Conventional Commit messages and maintaining a Release PR.

## How it works

- Scans git history for Conventional Commit messages since the last release
- Keeps a **Release PR** open and up-to-date with the changelog and version bump
- Merges the PR → creates the GitHub release and tag
- `fix:` → patch bump, `feat:` → minor bump, `feat!:` / `fix!:` → major bump

## Key inputs

| Input | Default | Notes |
|-------|---------|-------|
| `token` | `GITHUB_TOKEN` | Use a PAT or App token so triggered workflows run |
| `release-type` | — | Simple strategy (e.g. `simple`, `node`). Omit when using manifest config |
| `target-branch` | auto-detected | Branch to open the release PR against |
| `config-file` | `release-please-config.json` | Path to manifest config |
| `manifest-file` | `.release-please-manifest.json` | Path to versions manifest |
| `skip-github-release` | `false` | Set `true` to only create the PR, skip tagging |
| `skip-github-pull-request` | `false` | Set `true` to only tag, skip the PR |
| `skip-labeling` | `false` | Skip adding labels to the release PR |
| `release-as` | — | Force a specific version for the next release |

## Key outputs

| Output | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `prs_created` | `true` if a release PR was created or updated |
| `pr` | JSON of the PullRequest object |
| `releases_created` | `true` if any release was created |
| `release_created` | `true` for the root component release |
| `version` | Full semver value (e.g. `1.2.3`) |
| `major` / `minor` / `patch` | Individual semver components |
| `tag_name` | The created release tag |
| `sha` | SHA the release was tagged at |

For monorepos with `path`, outputs are prefixed: `<path>--release_created`, `<path>--version`, etc.

## Required workflow permissions

```yaml
permissions:
  contents: write
  pull-requests: write
```

## Advanced config (manifest mode)

Omit `release-type` and provide config/manifest files instead:

```yaml
- uses: googleapis/release-please-action@v4
  with:
    token: ${{ secrets.MY_TOKEN }}
    config-file: .github/release-please-config.json
    manifest-file: .github/.release-please-manifest.json
```

## Important: GITHUB_TOKEN limitation

Resources created by release-please (tags, PRs) **will not trigger** other GitHub Actions workflows when using the default `GITHUB_TOKEN`. Use a PAT or GitHub App token if downstream workflows need to run on release events.

## v3 → v4 migration

| Old `command` | v4 equivalent |
|---------------|---------------|
| `github-release` | `skip-github-pull-request: true` |
| `release-pr` | `skip-github-release: true` |
| `manifest` | omit `release-type` |
| `manifest-pr` | `skip-github-release: true` + omit `release-type` |
